From 0e9b58b58420d6ea2fe0698fc51716fd50d04120 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:53:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] doc/examples/extract_mvs: return a failure exit status
 without a video stream

main() ends with "return ret < 0", but ret is set to 1 when the input
has no video stream that can be decoded, so the exit status is 0:

    $ ./extract_mvs audio.mp2; echo $?
    ...
    Could not find video stream in the input, aborting
    0

Use a negative error code, as the other error paths do.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FZ4G6798n6Ua4qu6xwWu3S
---
 doc/examples/extract_mvs.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/doc/examples/extract_mvs.c b/doc/examples/extract_mvs.c
index b5ed2c5..73c8570 100644
--- a/doc/examples/extract_mvs.c
+++ b/doc/examples/extract_mvs.c
@@ -158,7 +158,7 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv)
 
     if (!video_stream) {
         fprintf(stderr, "Could not find video stream in the input, aborting\n");
-        ret = 1;
+        ret = AVERROR_STREAM_NOT_FOUND;
         goto end;
     }
 
